  ],
  "solution": "<p>The square root requires <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>, so equality forces <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math> can contain solutions.</p><p>Sketch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math> on this restricted domain. On <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math>, the cosine curve decreases from 3 to 0 while the square-root curve increases, giving one crossing. On the next positive cosine arch, the cosine curve starts below <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>, rises above it at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math> (since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>), then falls below it again. The sketch gives one crossing on each side of that arch.</p><p>There are no intersections on the remaining intervals because cosine is negative there. The total is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>. This follows the graph-counting approach of the official worked answer; the roots themselves need not be found.</p><p><strong>Answer D: 3 solutions.</strong></p>",
